bic_trace_step.reason:
In `xlog_ticket_get()` (near the end of the snippet), the padding for roundoff is calculated as:


/* for padding */
if (XFS_SB_VERSION_HASLOGV2(&log->l_mp->m_sb) &&
    log->l_mp->m_sb.sb_logsunit > 1) {
    /* log su roundoff */
    unit_bytes += log->l_mp->m_sb.sb_logsunit;  
} else {
    /* BB roundoff */
    unit_bytes += BBSIZE;
}


When no log stripe unit is specified (`sb_logsunit <= 1`), the code uses a hardcoded `BBSIZE` (512 bytes) for alignment, ignoring the log sector size (`sb_logsectsize`). This is exactly the vulnerable construct described in the root cause: a default roundoff of 512 bytes is used irrespective of the larger sector size, which can lead to log corruption. The fix (using `sb_logsectsize`) is not present.
